  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 159 AM MDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nOn Thursday and Friday, the area is still expected to be under\nan upper-level ridging pattern that amplifies towards the Great\nLakes region. while the ridge amplifies to the northeast, a\nbroad trough to the south-southwest begins moving to the east\nthat would put us into southwesterly flow aloft. With this being\nsaid, temperatures would likely remain above average staying in\nthe 70s. Some cloud coverage begins to build overnight as mid-\nto upper-level moisture passes over. Winds are still forecast to\npick up from 5-10 mph from Thursday to 20-25 mph Friday from the\nsouth. \n\nOver the weekend, the upper-level pattern changes into zonal\nflow once as the trough system steadily passes over the area.\nThis should bring a cold front early Saturday morning creating\nslight chances (30%) for showers over the entire forecast area \nuntil Sunday morning. With the chances of showers, there is some\ntiming uncertainty with the cold front and trough system as \nensemble guidance shows a continuing spread when it will pass \nover. If the trough speeds up, it would allow the cold front to\npass through Friday evening and bring chances for showers \novernight and into Saturday afternoon. However, if the the \ntrough slows down, this would then push the cold front to come \nin midday Saturday allowing showers to occur throughout the rest\nof the day and into Sunday morning. Once the cold front passes,\ntemperatures are forecast to be in the 60s with some clouds \nlingering around.",
